<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>NEO Close-Approach Tracker · RealAether</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Upcoming near-Earth object close approaches from NASA/JPL CNEOS, with an independent REBOUND check. Built by Geebs &amp; 3TH3R3AL1 — RealAether.">
  <meta property="og:type" content="website">
  <meta property="og:site_name" content="RealAether">
  <meta property="og:title" content="NEO Close-Approach Tracker — RealAether">
  <meta property="og:description" content="Upcoming near-Earth object close approaches from NASA/JPL CNEOS, with an independent REBOUND check. Built by Geebs &amp; 3TH3R3AL1 — RealAether.">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>NEO Close-Approach Tracker
      <small>RealAether · Forged in the Aether · CNEOS list, independent REBOUND check</small>
    </h1>
    <nav>
      <a href="../">← AetherWeather</a>
      <a href="../crrd/">Cosmic Ray Detector</a>
      <a href="#methods">Methods</a>
      <a class="support-top" href="https://ko-fi.com/realaether" target="_blank" rel="noopener">&#9733; Support</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main>
    <section class="card span8" id="next-card">
      <h2>Next Earth close approach</h2>
      <p id="next-loading" class="note">Loading catalog…</p>
      <div id="next-body" hidden>
        <p class="hero-name"><a id="next-name" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"></a></p>
        <div class="stats">
          <div class="stat"><b id="next-count" class="countdown big">—</b><span>Countdown (ET)</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b id="next-when">—</b><span id="next-tz">Date and time, ET 24-hour</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b id="next-dist">—</b><span>Distance</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b id="next-vel">—</b><span>Relative velocity</span></div>
          <div class="stat"><b id="next-size">—</b><span>Estimated size</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="note" id="next-note"></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card span4">
      <h2>Catalog snapshot</h2>
      <div class="stats" id="snap-stats"></div>
      <p class="note" id="snap-note">Times are America/New_York (Eastern, 24-hour). CNEOS source times are TDB and have been converted.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card span12">
      <h2>Upcoming flybys</h2>
      <div class="filters">
        <label>Body
          <select id="flt-body">
            <option value="Earth" selected>Earth</option>
            <option value="Moon">Moon</option>
            <option value="Mars">Mars</option>
            <option value="all">All three</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label>Window
          <select id="flt-window">
            <option value="90">Next 90 days</option>
            <option value="365" selected>Next 12 months</option>
            <option value="730">Next 24 months</option>
            <option value="all">Full 10-year list</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label>Search <input id="flt-q" type="search" placeholder="Name or designation" autocomplete="off"></label>
        <label><input id="flt-pha" type="checkbox"> PHAs only</label>
        <label><input id="flt-close" type="checkbox"> Within 0.01 au (~3.9 LD)</label>
        <span class="note" id="flt-count"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table id="flybys">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th data-key="fullname">Object</th>
              <th data-key="body">Body</th>
              <th data-key="jd_tdb">Date (ET)</th>
              <th class="num" data-key="dist_km">Distance (km)</th>
              <th class="num" data-key="dist_ld">Distance (LD)</th>
              <th class="num" data-key="v_rel_kms">v<sub>rel</sub> (km/s)</th>
              <th class="num" data-key="diameter_km">Size</th>
              <th class="num" data-key="h">H</th>
              <th data-key="pha">PHA</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Object names link to the official JPL SBDB page. Distances and times in this table are the CNEOS values, converted to Eastern Time and to km / lunar distances (1 LD = 384,400 km). Size is a JPL-measured diameter when one exists; otherwise it is estimated from absolute magnitude H (Fowler &amp; Chillemi 1992) with pV = 0.154, the CNEOS Sentry convention, and a typical albedo range of 0.05–0.25 shown on hover. Click a row to sketch its orbit.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card span6" id="validation">
      <h2>Independent engine vs NASA</h2>
      <div class="stats" id="val-stats"></div>
      <p class="note" id="val-note"></p>
      <div class="table-wrap" style="max-height:360px;margin-top:10px">
        <table id="val-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th data-key="fullname">Object</th>
              <th data-key="datetime_et">Date (ET)</th>
              <th class="num" data-key="cneos_km">CNEOS (km)</th>
              <th class="num" data-key="pred_km">Ours (km)</th>
              <th class="num" data-key="ddist_km">Δ km</th>
              <th class="num" data-key="dt_minutes">Δ min</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="card span6">
      <h2>Orbit sketch</h2>
      <div class="filters">
        <label>Object <select id="orbit-select"></select></label>
        <label>Mark
          <select id="orbit-mark">
            <option value="ca" selected>Position at close approach</option>
            <option value="now">Position now (Keplerian)</option>
          </select>
        </label>
      </div>
      <canvas id="orbit-canvas" width="720" height="520" aria-label="Top-down inner solar system orbit sketch"></canvas>
      <div class="legend">
        <span><i style="background:#f3d36b"></i>Sun</span>
        <span><i style="background:#9aa0b8"></i>Mercury, Venus</span>
        <span><i style="background:#5ad1ff"></i>Earth</span>
        <span><i style="background:#e08a6a"></i>Mars</span>
        <span><i style="background:#d4af37"></i>Selected NEO</span>
      </div>
      <p class="note">Top-down ecliptic J2000 view of the inner solar system. Planet rings are circular at their mean distances, for scale. The NEO path is a Keplerian ellipse from the JPL SBDB osculating elements — a sketch, not the N-body validation on the left.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="card span12" id="methods">
      <h2>Methods &amp; data</h2>
      <p class="note">
        This page is a static section of RealAether, intended to live at
        <code>realaether/impact/</code> on GitHub Pages. The upcoming-flyby list
        is taken from the
        <a href="https://ssd-api.jpl.nasa.gov/doc/cad.html">JPL SBDB Close-Approach Data API (CNEOS)</a>,
        which is authoritative. Orbital elements and physical parameters come from the
        <a href="https://ssd-api.jpl.nasa.gov/doc/sbdb_query.html">JPL SBDB Query API</a>.
        Objects currently on the
        <a href="https://cneos.jpl.nasa.gov/sentry/">Sentry</a> risk list are flagged, but this tracker is not an impact-risk product — Sentry is.
        Our REBOUND + DE440s N-body engine (IAS15, first-order GR, Earth and Moon separate) independently re-integrates a subset:
        every upcoming Earth approach within 0.01 au, the 200 closest, and every condition-code-0 upcoming Earth approach.
        It does not re-integrate all 43,000+ NEOs, because CNEOS already searched that catalog. The engine does not include Earth J2, Yarkovsky, or asteroid perturbers.
        Civil times are converted from CNEOS TDB to America/New_York. No home address or local network information is published here.
      </p>
      <p class="note" id="src-note"></p>
    </section>
  </main>

